  "summary": {
    "plain": "With 2.82 years of data and a 1 keV threshold, COSINE-100 fitted yearly-modulation amplitudes of 0.0067 +/- 0.0042 (1-6 keV) and 0.0051 +/- 0.0047 (2-6 keV) counts per day per kg per keV, for a phase fixed at 152.5 days.",
    "technical": "Live time 2.82 yr, active mass 61.3 kg, exposure 173 kg yr; improved event selection (threshold 1 keV) and time-dependent background model; the abstract says the experiment 'aims to test DAMA/LIBRA's claim of dark matter discovery' (Phys. Rev. D 106, 052005 (2022))."
  },
  "title": "Three-year annual modulation search with COSINE-100",
